Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-06-11
Subject: Make tnode equality a nil-safe class function
License: expat

`tnode.isequal` is written as a two-node predicate: it treats two nil nodes as equal, treats one nil node as unequal, and only then dispatches to `docompare` on the left operand.  Keeping that operation as an instance method makes call sites such as `tempinfo^.withnode.isequal(...)` rely on a nil receiver being callable.

That is valid for this Pascal source, but it has no valid C++ member-call spelling: a translated `nullptr->p_isequal(...)` call has undefined behavior before the method body can test the receiver.  The FPC 3.2.0 bootstrap reaches that path while comparing optional AST children during the RTL `sysutils` build.

Make equality an explicit static class function over `(left,right)` and update callers to use that form.  The nil handling stays in one place and the non-nil path still uses `left.docompare(right)`, so subclass comparison dispatch is preserved without using a nil method receiver.

